Main requirement
Students should not simply install programs and take screenshots. They must
explain what they installed, why they installed it, how they configured it, what
problems they encountered, and how

During this mini-project, I learned how to prepare a computer for everyday professional use. I learned how to check computer hardware and identify driver problems using Device Manager. I also learned how to install and configure device drivers and verify that devices work correctly after installation.

Another important part of the project was installing and configuring office applications. I practiced working with a word processor, spreadsheet application and presentation software. I created test files and configured basic application settings.

I also learned how to check and configure computer security. I checked Windows Security, antivirus protection, firewall settings and security updates. I learned why real-time protection and regular security scans are important for protecting a computer from threats.

The most difficult part of the project was identifying and solving configuration problems. Troubleshooting required checking the system carefully and choosing appropriate solutions instead of simply reinstalling software.

The project helped me understand that a computer technician should not only install software but also test the system, solve problems and document the results. In the future, I would take screenshots during every important step and record driver and software versions immediately to make the final documentation more accurate.
